> Finite arithmetic, explicit failures and owned capture

The product form of the secant can overflow even for finite endpoints and
finite callback values. The shared kernel retains that expression when checks
prove its products, differences and division finite. Otherwise it forms a
positive weight ratio after scaling and uses std::lerp, avoiding the overflowing
products or sum. Nonzero secant products that become subnormal or zero also
select that fallback, preventing a spurious endpoint trial from product underflow.
Ordinary underflow flags can still occur while detecting those products or
halving a weight. The ratio or final point can still round to an endpoint;
that produces a stagnation stop unless an earlier stopping test passes.
The huge-coordinate example below has ordinary floating interpolation error,
so its small measured residual is printed rather than called exact.

Actual endpoint values remain distinct from artificial weights. If an actual
Illinois halving underflows a nonzero weight to zero, execution stops explicitly
without interpreting that artificial zero as a callback root. A finite jump
between adjacent doubles illustrates a separate issue: coordinate tolerance
can pass without a zero of a discontinuous mathematical function.

Input callbacks, finite endpoints, supported policies, finite nonnegative
new-option tolerances and a positive trial budget are validated before work.
The legacy tolerance remains strictly positive. Nonfinite callback returns
raise a domain error; callback exceptions propagate. Both endpoint calls are
retained in input order, even when the first value is zero.

Optional capture counts whole records: C=E+K=2+2K for K actual trials,
including two endpoint evaluation records and one evaluation plus one step
per trial. The default quota is one million; zero disables only that quota.
The initial two records are admitted before either callback, and each next
pair before interpolation or its callback. Output, metadata, capacities,
allocator bytes and runtime temporaries are excluded, so C is not peak RAM.
Ordinary calls keep no optional history or quota. Exceptions return no partial
trace, and returned record copies own their values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/false_position_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <cfenv>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  volatile double maximum=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();const double M=maximum;std::print("| finite stress case | root | actual residual | trials | guarded trials | overflow or invalid flag |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");for(int which=0;which<2;++which){auto f=[=](double x){return which?(M*.75)*(x-.25):x/M-.25;};std::feclearexcept(FE_ALL_EXCEPT);const auto r=dm::algorithms::false_position_work(f,which?-1:-M,which?1:M);const bool bad=std::fetestexcept(FE_OVERFLOW|FE_INVALID);std::print("| {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {} | {} | {} |\n",which?"huge callback values":"huge coordinates",r.result.root,r.result.residual,r.result.iterations,r.guarded_interpolations,bad);if(!r.result.converged||bad||r.guarded_interpolations!=1)throw std::runtime_error("finite guard failed");}
  dm::algorithms::FalsePositionOptions tiny_options;tiny_options.residual_tolerance=0;const double tiny=std::ldexp(1.,-1020);const auto tiny_result=dm::algorithms::false_position_work([=](double x){return (x/tiny-.25)*tiny;},-tiny,tiny,tiny_options);std::print("\nTiny affine: root/scale {}; trials {}; guarded trials {}; stop {}.\n",tiny_result.result.root/tiny,tiny_result.result.iterations,tiny_result.guarded_interpolations,dm::algorithms::false_position_stop_name(tiny_result.stop));if(!tiny_result.result.converged||tiny_result.result.root/tiny!=.25||tiny_result.guarded_interpolations==0)throw std::runtime_error("tiny-product interpolation failed");
  dm::algorithms::FalsePositionOptions o;o.residual_tolerance=0;const double a=1,b=std::nextafter(a,2.);auto jump=[=](double x){return x==a?-1.:1.;};const auto stagnated=dm::algorithms::false_position_work(jump,a,b,o);o.x_tolerance=1e-10;const auto interval=dm::algorithms::false_position_work(jump,a,b,o);o.x_tolerance=0;o.max_iterations=10;const double small=std::numeric_limits<double>::denorm_min();const auto underflow=dm::algorithms::false_position_trace([=](double x){return x==-M?-small:small;},-M,M,o);
  std::size_t calls=0;auto linear=[&](double x){++calls;return x-1;};int rejected=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::false_position_trace(linear,0,2,{},1);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}const auto initial_calls=calls;try{(void)dm::algorithms::false_position_trace(linear,0,2,{},3);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}const auto endpoint_calls=calls;auto exact=dm::algorithms::false_position_trace(linear,0,2,{},4);const auto owned=exact;exact.steps.front().estimate=99;const auto disabled=dm::algorithms::false_position_trace(linear,0,2,{},0);
  std::print("\nAdjacent finite jump: no-tolerance stop {}; coordinate-tolerance stop {}; actual residuals {} and {}.\n",dm::algorithms::false_position_stop_name(stagnated.stop),dm::algorithms::false_position_stop_name(interval.stop),stagnated.result.residual,interval.result.residual);std::print("Actual weight underflow: trials {}; halvings {}; callbacks {}; capture {}; stop {}; converged {}.\n",underflow.outcome.result.iterations,underflow.outcome.weight_halvings,underflow.outcome.evaluations,underflow.captured_entries,dm::algorithms::false_position_stop_name(underflow.outcome.stop),underflow.outcome.result.converged);std::print("Quota controls: initial-short calls {}; trial-short cumulative calls {}; rejections {}/2; exact capture {}; disabled capture {}; owned estimate {}.\n",initial_calls,endpoint_calls,rejected,owned.captured_entries,disabled.captured_entries,owned.steps.front().estimate);
  int invalid=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::false_position({},0,2);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::false_position([](double x){return x-1;},0,2,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::false_position([](double){return std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();},0,2);}catch(const std::domain_error&){++invalid;}std::print("Malformed/nonfinite rejections {}/3.\n",invalid);
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(58,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.7;box.height=2.1;box.font_size=23;box.fill={191,219,254};g.node("calls",{0,0},"Actual callback records\n2 endpoints + K trials\nfinite values only",box);box.fill={187,247,208};g.node("steps",{6.5,0},"Actual step records\nK weighted secants\ntrue values retained",box);box.fill={254,215,170};g.node("capture",{13,0},"Optional capture\nC = 2 + 2K\nwhole records",box).text({6.5,3.2},"Admission before work; explicit numerical stops; owned snapshots",25).save_svg("build/false_position_limits.svg");if(rejected!=2||invalid!=3||initial_calls!=0||endpoint_calls!=2||owned.steps.front().estimate!=1||underflow.outcome.stop!=dm::algorithms::FalsePositionStop::WeightUnderflow)throw std::runtime_error("boundary controls failed");
}
